"""Lecture 35 objective pool B -- Asthma: diagnosis (history, examination, spirometry, provocation and
other tests, peak flow), severity classification, differential diagnosis and allergic bronchopulmonary
aspergillosis (slides 44-65).

KEYS ARE WRITTEN SHORT ON PURPOSE -- detail lives in the explanation.
EXPLANATIONS follow tools/question_writing/EXPLAIN_DEEP.md (2026-10-29).

Set 1 is recall against the syllabus objectives, so no stem carries a patient age. The s62 severity table
is the "12 years of age and older" table; its age-normal ratio column is never keyed ("I'm not going to ask
you ... that the number I give you is normal for an 80-year-old"). Bronchodilator response is keyed as 12
percent only (s53).
"""
